===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or pertaining to a [[dystopia]].
#* {{quote-web|en|date=22 March 2012|author=Scott Tobias|work=AV Club|title=The Hunger Games|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/the-hunger-games,71293/|passage=If Suzanne Collins’ novel The Hunger Games turns up on middle-school curricula 50 years from now—and as accessible '''dystopian''' science fiction with allusions to early-21st-century strife, that isn’t out of the question—the lazy students of the future can be assured that they can watch the movie version and still get better than a passing grade.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Philip Oltermann|url=http://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jun/30/german-scifi-fans-reading-dystopia-brexit-britain|title=German sci-fi fans lap up dystopian tales of Brexit Britain|date=2019-06-30|work=The Guardian|quotee=Tom Hillenbrand|passage=In my book Britain has actually worked out how it wants to leave and the EU is preparing a new constitution as a result. The real Brexit is actually much more '''dystopian'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2020-01-17|author=Amy Chozick|title=This Is the Guy Who’s Taking Away the Likes|work=New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/01/17/business/instagram-likes.html|passage=He kept thinking about an episode of “Black Mirror,” the British '''dystopian''' anthology series, in which the characters rate everyone they interact with on a scale of 1 to 5 stars. (It doesn’t end well.)}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Samira Asma-Sadeque|title=‘It’s too much’: New Yorkers don masks or stay inside amid smog crisis|work=The Guardian|date=2023-06-07|url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/07/new-york-city-wildfire-smoke-air-quality-mask|issn=0261-3077|passage=The whole city is immersed in a '''dystopian'''-looking smog: urban streets in sepia, emptier than usual, bathed in an eerie quiet.}}
# [[dire|Dire]]; characterized by human [[suffering]] or [[misery]].

